{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 31,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I Made a covenant with my eyes; why then should I think upon a maid?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For what portion of God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is there",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " from above? and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "what",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " inheritance of the Almighty from on high?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not destruction to the wicked? and a strange ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "punishment",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the workers of iniquity?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Doth not he see my ways, and count all my steps?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have walked with vanity, or if my foot hath hasted to deceit;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let me be weighed in an even balance, that God may know my integrity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If my step hath turned out of the way, and my heart walked after my eyes, and if any blot hath cleaved to my hands;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " let me sow, and let another eat; yes, let my offspring be rooted out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If my heart hath been deceived by a woman, or ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "if",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I have laid wait at my neighbor's door;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " let my wife grind to another, and let others bow down upon her.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a hainous crime; yea, it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an iniquity ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be punished by",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the judges.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a fire ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " consumeth to destruction, and would root out all my increase.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I despised the cause of my man-servant or of my maid-servant, when they contended with me;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What then shall I do when God riseth up? and when he visiteth, what shall I answer him?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Did not he that made me in the womb make him? and did not one fashion us in the womb?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have withheld the poor from ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "their",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " desire, or have caused the eyes of the widow to fail;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Or have eaten my morsel myself alone, and the fatherless hath not eaten of it;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(For from my youth he was brought up with me, as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "with",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a father, and I have guided her from my mother's womb;)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have seen any perish for want of clothing, or any poor without covering;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If his loins have not blessed me, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "if",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " he hath not been warmed with the fleece of my sheep;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have lifted up my hand against the fatherless, when I saw my help in the gate:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " let my arm fall from my shoulder-blade, and my arm be broken from the bone.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For destruction ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "from",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a terror to me, and by reason of his highness I could not endure.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have made gold my hope, or have said to the fine gold, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "Thou art",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my confidence;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have rejoiced because my wealth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " great, and because my hand had gained much;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have beheld the sun when it shined, or the moon walking ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " brightness;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And my heart hath been secretly enticed, or my mouth hath kissed my hand:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This also ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an iniquity ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be punished by",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the judge: for I should have denied the God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " above.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have rejoiced at the destruction of him that hated me, or have lifted up myself when evil found him:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Neither have I suffered my mouth to sin by wishing a curse to his soul.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If the men of my tabernacle have not said, Oh that we had of his flesh! we cannot be satisfied.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The stranger did not lodge in the street: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "but",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I opened my doors to the traveler.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have covered my transgressions as Adam, by hiding my iniquity in my bosom:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Did I fear a great multitude, or did the contempt of families terrify me, that I kept silence, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " went not out of the door?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh that one would hear me! behold, my desire ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the Almighty would answer me, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " my adversary had written a book.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Surely I would take it upon my shoulder, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bind it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a crown to me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I would declare to him the number of my steps; as a prince would I go near to him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If my land crieth against me, or its furrows likewise complain;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I have eaten the fruits of it without money, or have caused its owners to lose their life:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.31.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JOB.31.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let thistles grow instead of wheat, and cockle instead of barley. The words of Job are ended.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
